// atan2_safety.gen -- GenExpr atan2 verification for ideas/f_tensorfield.md
// Open Question 6 / ideas/f_weave_orientation_blend.md Fix B:
//
//   1. Does atan2 compile and run in a jit.gl.pix codebox on this GPU?
//   2. Does it return the mathematically correct value (branch, quadrant,
//      range) when its inputs come from a *sampled texture* (the decode
//      use case), not just from analytic coords?
//   3. Is the branch cut continuous from the sampled side -- i.e. do the
//      pixels adjacent to the cut, sampled through the same bilinear
//      path the consumers will use, return values consistent with the
//      analytic value at the *pixel center* rather than something the
//      sampling interpolated across the cut?
//   4. Are the tensor-decode-specific patterns safe: the half-angle
//      decode theta = 0.5*atan2(b, a) (range (-pi/2, pi/2], the known
//      vertical-axis wrap concern) and the doubled re-check
//      atan2(sin(2t), cos(2t)) == t mod pi (round trip)?
//
// Input in1: a vecfield texture, RG = F*0.5 + 0.5 (the f_vecfield
// convention). Every pixel encodes a distinct direction covering all four
// quadrants densely; the bench script lays it out so every atan2 quadrant
// boundary lands strictly inside texels.
//
// Outputs, packed into out1 RGBA:
//   R = theta          = atan2(Fy, Fx)  mapped to [0,1) by /2pi + 0.5
//   G = half-angle     = 0.5*theta      mapped by /pi + 0.5   (fix-B shape)
//   B = round trip     = atan2(sin(theta), cos(theta))/2pi + 0.5
//   A = quadrant probe = sign(Fx) mapped as (sign+1)/2, cross-check

F = (sample(in1, norm) - 0.5) * 2;
theta = atan2(F.y, F.x);
out1 = vec(theta / 6.283185307179586 + 0.5,
           theta * 0.5 / 3.141592653589793 + 0.5,
           atan2(sin(theta), cos(theta)) / 6.283185307179586 + 0.5,
           (sign(F.x) + 1) * 0.5);